% The table of integer values is charged to the memory limit with the
% relations, whether a program states an integer or evaluation computes
% it.  Counting to two thousand interns every integer on the way: the
% relation holding them takes some 25000 bytes and the integers' table some
% 37000, so a limit of 50000 admits the relation and not the two.
n(0).
n(Y) :- n(X), X < 2000, Y = X + 1.

n(2000)?
